(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// Functions, built-in functions, cells, code objects and modules."] [8 2 "// MethodDescrType is method_descriptor (descrobject.c's PyMethodDescr_Type): a built-in type's method as its class"] [9 2 "// holds it (list.append), a *Builtin with an Owner and no Self (queue 286: multiprocessing.reduction registers its"] [10 2 "// method descriptors' reducer for type(list.append), which was builtin_function_or_method, so ForkingPickler asked"] [11 2 "// every built-in function it pickled for an __objclass__)"] [18 1 "// Function is a Python function: a code object with its globals, defaults and closure"] [19 1 "// (CPython's PyFunctionObject)."] [26 20 "// positional defaults, or nil"] [27 20 "// keyword-only defaults, or nil"] [29 20 "// __annotate__, or nil"] [30 20 "// __type_params__, or nil"] [31 20 "// __dict__, made on first use"] [34 2 "// GlobalsMap is the globals when FunctionType(code, globals) was given a dict subclass's instance (queue 205f:"] [35 2 "// annotationlib's _StringifierDict), Globals its dict: the function's global loads go through its __getitem__"] [36 2 "// (CPython's LOAD_GLOBAL on non-exact globals, PyMapping_GetOptionalItem: its __missing__), nil for a dict"] [42 1 "// Builtin is a function implemented in Go (CPython's builtin_function_or_method)."] [46 14 "// the bound object of a method, or nil"] [47 2 "// objectDescr: object's method that left object's dict through the class (methodDescrs[b] is ObjectType)"] [49 2 "// wakeup: a task's task_wakeup, a node of finalize.go's graph (a pending task's cycle runs through it)"] [51 2 "// Owner is the type a method of a built-in type's dict belongs to (d_type, m_class's); unchecked: a class or"] [52 2 "// static method, its first argument no instance of Owner"] [64 1 "// isMethodDescr: b is a method descriptor (a built-in type's method, unbound; method_descriptor)."] [67 1 "// Cell is a closure's cell; Value nil is empty (unbound)."] [72 1 "// CodeObject is a code object as a Python value (the IR's {:code ...} constants)."] [77 1 "// Module is a module: its name and namespace."] [81 2 "// Cls is a subclass of module this module is an instance of (six's _LazyModule, queue 205), nil for module itself"] [83 2 "// slots are a subclass's __slots__' values (queue 226)"] [94 1 "// builtinFuncModules are the built-in modules' functions' modules (PY6d's REQUEST: a function's __module__,"] [95 1 "// CPython's m_module, which pickle saves it by)."] [112 4 "// method_vectorcall's check: a method descriptor called with its instance first"] [121 37 "// one allocation (queue 210: append grew it a second time)"] [126 4 "// method_check_args (PY7: dict.update() was a Go panic, test_ordered_dict's"] [127 4 "// CPythonBuiltinDictTests.test_update)"] [134 2 "// meth_richcompare: the same function of the same object; meth_hash not from the object's own hash"] [154 62 "// meth_repr"] [157 41 "// meth_repr of tp_new_wrapper's builtin, bound to its type"] [162 2 "// method_descriptor (queue 286): called as a method descriptor is (BuiltinType's call slot checks the instance),"] [163 2 "// method_repr, method_get (descr_check: the instance's type, the class's own as the class is asked), descr_reduce"] [193 2 "// builtin_function_or_method's __module__ (PY6d's REQUEST): a module's function's module, a builtin's"] [194 2 "// \"builtins\", else None (pickle's whichmodule then finds the function in sys.modules)"] [195 2 "// a built-in method named like a slot (a generator's __next__) has the slot wrapper's doc (typeobject.c's slotdefs)"] [219 2 "// methodobject.c's meth_reduce (PY6d's REQUEST: pickle saves a built-in function by name): a function's"] [220 2 "// qualified name, a bound method as getattr(self, name)"] [236 3 "// CPython's \"at 0x...\", the address an identity number (asyncio's Handle reprs and their tests: PY6h's"] [237 3 "// REQUEST, queue 200)"] [246 2 "// cell([contents]): Objects/cellobject.c's cell_new, cell_repr and cell_richcompare (queue 205f: annotationlib's"] [247 2 "// _build_closure makes the stringifiers' cells)"] [268 35 "// tp_richcompare without tp_hash: hash() refuses a cell"] [278 3 "// empty cells come before anything else (cell_compare_impl)"] [304 3 "// module_repr: importlib's _module_repr once importlib is the import system (PY6b's request)"] [310 4 "// importlib's _module_repr: a module with a location is \"from\" it"] [315 2 "// module(name, doc=None), CPython's module_init; a subclass's instance (queue 205: six's _MovedItems) made empty"] [316 2 "// as new_module makes it, its __init__ (module.__init__ through super()) filling it"] [339 2 "// module_new: an uninitialized module (its dict empty), any arguments; module_init fills it"] [355 2 "// module_getsets: __annotations__ and __annotate__ (PEP 649), data descriptors before the dict"] [360 38 "// a subclass's instance: its class's data descriptors first"] [386 2 "// module.__dir__ (module_dir, queue 223: traceback's suggestions call it): the dict's __dir__ function called,"] [387 2 "// else the dict's keys"] [407 1 "// functionNew is function(code, globals, name=None, argdefs=None, closure=None, kwdefaults=None), types.FunctionType"] [408 1 "// called: Objects/funcobject.c's func_new (its clinic's argument checks, then func_new_impl's in its order, and their"] [409 1 "// messages) over PyFunction_New (the code's name, qualname and docstring, the globals' __name__ as __module__, the"] [410 1 "// builtins from the globals' __builtins__). Queue 205f: annotationlib's FORWARDREF and STRING formats call an"] [411 1 "// __annotate__'s code with a _StringifierDict as its globals (typing.NamedTuple's annotated classes, pip's import)."] [477 2 "// _PyEval_BuiltinsFromGlobals: the globals' __builtins__ (a module its dict), else the running frame's"] [497 19 "// PyFunction_EVENT_CREATE (queue 274)"] [502 1 "// moduleGetAttr is module_getattro (_Py_module_getattro_impl): suppress is its argument, 1 when the lookup is"] [503 1 "